{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/647336-kinain-fae-blood-and-faerie-affinity","id":647336,"title":"Kinain, Fae Blood and Faerie Affinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T15:59:02-07:00","id":647336,"title":"Kinain, Fae Blood and Faerie Affinity","content":"Okay, so there's some conflicting info about how best to handle kinain (especially kinain who are also mages or Garou, etc).<br /> <br /> The Enchanted sets out a system for otherwise mortal/human kinain. The Fae Blood Merit exists in multiple gamelines but is vague. Faerie Affinity is also another Merit, but one which just seems to make relations with the fae easier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm running a Changeling/Mage crossover game, and I've been acutely aware of in-game and systems-based ways of facilitating cooperation. One of my new players wants to play a kinain mage, so I'm trying to give them a fair system that doesn't make them overpowered but which does give them a few low-powered perks. I want this kind of character because it works in the game I want to run, but I want to avoid Samuel Haight syndrome too.<br /> <br /> Here's the stuff I wrote for the wiki. Can anyone offer any feedback?<br /> <br /> Glamour and cantrips: Sorcerers, psychics and mages can all be kinain. However, only unawakened kinain may use cantrips (Arts or Realms). An Awakened mage cannot have a Glamour rating (because being tied to the Dreaming would prevent their Avatar from Awakening). Any Fae Gift or Background that requires the use of Glamour is therefore off-limits to mage characters (Fith-Fath, Riastradh, etc).<br /> <br /> Mages can mimic cantrips as in-paradigm rotes using their Spheres. Taking Fae Gifts requires taking the Faerie Blood Merit as precursor.<br /> <br /> Character creation: The character creation rules in The Enchanted are for mortal kinain only. You should create your character as a mage or hedge mage first, and then use Freebies to 'add on' the fae characteristics. You should consult The Enchanted for the specific rules on kinain-specific traits.<br /> <br /> Apply the following template to modify your kinain character:<br /> <br /> 1. Create a mage/hedge mage character as normal, remembering that chimerical reality and/or their fae blood will be incorporated into their paradigm. The character's Avatar essence might also be informed by their fae heritage (a Sluagh-descended kinain may be Primordial, while a Satyr's relative may be Dynamic).<br /> <br /> 2. Take the 4-point Merit: Faerie Blood. This will grant the character a single dot in the Faerie Blood Background. Alternatively, you can take the Faerie Affinity Merit, which gives you a lower Banality (one dot lower than normal) and makes changelings more friendly, but does not allow the character to take any Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds, nor to interact with chimerical reality.<br /> <br /> 3. Note your Seeming and Seelie/Unseelie Legacies. Pick a Heritage (Kith). Your Banality rating will be the lower of: a) the Banality rating for your Seeming in The Enchanted; or b) the Banality rating as defined in the Character Creation for Mages section.<br /> <br /> 4. You start with no free Fae Gifts or Kinain Backgrounds. You can spend Freebies to take any Fae Gifts and Kinain Backgrounds you like (provided you already have the Faerie Blood Merit), but you may not take more dots in either of these than you have dots in the Faerie Blood Background. So if you have Faerie Blood 5, you can take up to five separate Fae Gifts and up to five separate Kinain Backgrounds. These tricks are Paradox-free. Kinain Backgrounds can only be bought from your Freebie pool, rather than from your normal Background dots.<br /> <br /> 5. Fae Marks can be taken to gain additional Freebie Points.<br /> <br /> The Kinain Background Fith-Fath costs 1-5 points (based on the dice pool for Fith-Fath) and can only be taken by hedge mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-31-2015, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T10:14:31-07:00","id":652742,"title":"","content":"I`d actually allow my awakend players to learn Cantrips and deal with Glamour.<br /> It`s really not that powerful and to top it all of, it would take a tremendous amound of experience-points to get it to useful levels. These are all points they cannot spend on their own magic, so in the end, they would lose just as much if not more, than what they gain. But if they wish to learn all that baggage.... :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:12:45-07:00","id":653047,"title":"","content":"One of the <i>Changeling</i> books, <b>Freeholds and Hidden Glens</b>, depicts a shared node/freehold (Terabithea) at UC Santa Cruz, held jointly by changelings and a local group of mages (mostly Verbena). It won't help with the kinain issue (the mages in question are all 100% human), but it still might give you some ideas for your own campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:53:46-07:00","id":656879,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys. You're probably right. Cantrips probably don't break the system that much. I actually have that book too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}